From 7453a979fa4963af2950e961a352aa123f216c16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:02:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] memories: a placed netlist's cells are dont_touch as well as
 FIRM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FIRM keeps the legaliser off the generator's cells; nothing kept the
resizer off them. repair_design on XiangShan's planned parent upsized
378 address inverters of the three placed register files in place,
INVx1 to INVx2, and the wider master overlapped its fixed neighbour, so
detailed placement passed its legalisation and failed check_placement.
The cells are final by construction: mark them dont_touch when they are
placed. Buffers that a repair adds around the array are new cells and
stay allowed.

Not upstreamed (builds on carried patch 0078). Retires with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 flow/scripts/structured_netlists.tcl | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/flow/scripts/structured_netlists.tcl b/flow/scripts/structured_netlists.tcl
index 6436b63bb..3c1fa63f8 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/structured_netlists.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/structured_netlists.tcl
@@ -92,6 +92,18 @@ if { 1 } {
         $inst setOrient $orient
         $inst setLocation [expr { $X + $cx - $dx0 }] [expr { $Y + $cy - $dy0 }]
         $inst setPlacementStatus FIRM
+        # The generator's cell is final: FIRM keeps the legaliser off it,
+        # dont_touch keeps the resizer off it. Without the second,
+        # repair_design upsizes an inverter in place, the wider master
+        # overlaps its fixed neighbour, and check_placement fails the stage
+        # (take 23: 378 address inverters, INVx1 -> INVx2). Buffers the
+        # repair adds around the array are new cells and stay allowed.
+        # The flops are excepted: CTS has to rewire their clock pins and a
+        # dont_touch instance refuses (ODB-0370); their outputs drive the
+        # short read-mux nets, which the repair has no reason to resize.
+        if { ![[$inst getMaster] isSequential] } {
+          $inst setDoNotTouch 1
+        }
         incr n
       }
       close $pf
